  "worked_solution": "We must express the given series in the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ denotes the first term of the series, $r$ denotes the common ratio, and $N$ denotes the number of terms in the series. In this case, ${a}_{1}=-1$ and $N=4.$\n\nTo find $r,$ we calculate the ratio of the first two terms in the series:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{3}{-1}=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, expressing the given geometric series in sigma notation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1+3-9+27 & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{4}(-1)\\cdot (-3)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
